**Gate failure fixed.** Two causes, both in the worker's harness directory, both resolved:

1. `tools/browser-harness/fixtures.mts` was unformatted — reformatted with `pnpm exec oxfmt`.
2. A new harness file was not in any TypeScript project, so type-aware lint reported 24 `error`-type warnings (exactly the failure mode `AGENTS.md` warns about). I changed `tools/tsconfig.json` to include `browser-harness/**/*.mts` as a glob, so a new file can never fall outside the project again. The worker has been told to keep the glob and to run format, typecheck, and lint after every write.

